      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, ok, I didn\u0027t realize that. The javadocs for them don\u0027t mention that distinction, only that we should use `check()` in cases where we want the exception thrown (and used by something higher in the call stack) and we should use `test()` in cases where we just want the business logic.\n\nI think if we care about the auditing, then we\u0027re going to need to review all the other places `test()` is already used. If that\u0027s not a requirement, then I think this change generally makes the code easier to understand and we should try to get it merged.",
